yword`? In Elasticsearch, a range query on a text field (analyzed) operates on the analyzed tokens. \\\"response\\\" is of string type — in Kibana, \\\"string\\\" usually means a text field with a .keyword subfield. Range on text fields is possible (applied to the tokens). Since each value is a single token like \\\"500\\\", the range \\\"500\\\"–\\\"599\\\" should work. But to be safer, use `response.keyword` with a range query — range queries on keyword fields are well supported.\\n\\nThe example of the .es-query rule's parameters:\\n{\\\"searchType\\\": \\\"esQuery\\\", \\\"esQuery\\\": \\\"{\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"match_all\\\\\\\":{}}}\\\", \\\"index\\\": [\\\"my-index\\\"], \\\"timeField\\\": \\\"@timestamp\\\", \\\"threshold\\\": [0], \\\"thresholdComparator\\\": \\\">\\\", \\\"timeWindowSize\\\": 5, \\\"timeWindowUnit\\\": \\\"m\\\", \\\"size\\\": 100}\\n\\nSo:\\n- searchType: \\\"esQuery\\\"\\n- esQuery: JSON string: {\\\"query\\\":{\\\"range\\\":{\\\"response.keyword\\\":{\\\"gte\\\":\\\"500\\\",\\\"lte\\\":\\\"599\\\"}}}}\\n- index: [\\\"kibana_sample_data_logs\\\"]\\n- timeField: \\\"timestamp\\\"\\n- threshold: [10]\\n- thresholdComparator: \\\">\\\"\\n- timeWindowSize: 5\\n- timeWindowUnit: \\\"m\\\"\\n- size: 100\\n- schedule_interval: \\\"1m\\\"\\n\\nCreate it in a disabled state (the default), and then enable it.\\n\\nAfter that, step 4: edit the response code panel (panel_index 1) and change its title to \\\"Responses by code\\\". Then read the rule back with get_alert_rule.\\n\\nFirst, let's create the rule.\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"I've created the dashboard with 2 panels and now I'm setting up an alert rule to fire when response codes in the 500–599 range exceed 10 occurrences in a 5-minute window.\\n\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"name\": \"create_alert_rule\", \"arguments\": {\"name\": \"LOC-c8ade4c5 5xx errors\", \"rule_type_id\": \".es-query\", \"consumer\": \"stackAlerts\", \"params\": {\"searchType\": \"esQu